==Trivia==
*His Japanese name, Tech Nolo-jiji (テク・ノロ爺, ''Teku・Noro-jiji''), is a pun on ''technology'' and 爺 ''jiji'', meaning "grandpa" or "old man" and similar in usage to the English words ''geezer'' and ''gramps''.
*His Korean name, Tech Nolo G (테크 놀로 G ''Tekeu Nollo G''), is a combination of ''technology'' and ''[[Red EnerG]]''.
*The first-person pronoun he uses in his Japanese description, ''washi'' (ワシ), is mainly used by men in Western Japan and stereotypical old men or [[wikipedia:Kansai|Kansaian]] characters in fiction.
*His hairstyle and mustache are reminiscent of [[wikipedia:Albert Einstein|Albert Einstein]]. His [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]] trait and Warp ability could allude to Einstein's [[wikipedia:Theory of relativity|theory of relativity]], while the fact that he is a variant of [[H. Nah]] may be a subtle reference to Einstein's formula for [[wikipedia:mass–energy equivalence|mass-energy equivalence]], E=mc^2, as H. Nah's Japanese name is High Energy (ハイ・エナジー). Lastly, the electricity in his attack animation combined with the participation trophy in his description could refer to how Einstein won the Nobel Prize in Physics for his explanation of the [[wikipedia:Photoelectric effect|photoelectric effect]].
**He also faintly resembles [[wikipedia:Karol Pollak|Karol Pollak]] and [[wikipedia:Charles Algernon Parsons|Charles Algernon Parsons]], both of which would fit with the electricity in his attack animation, but Albert Einstein is the closest match.

